Subject: Take a reference to the enum case an unserialized enum refers to
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

zend_enum_get_case() returns the case object borrowed from the class
constant. Storing it without a reference drops the case below its owners,
so the constant table later releases a freed object.

--- a/msgpack_unpack.c
+++ b/msgpack_unpack.c
@@ -693,7 +693,7 @@
 #else
                     ce = msgpack_unserialize_class(container, Z_STR_P(key), 0);
                     zend_object *enum_instance = zend_enum_get_case(ce, Z_STR_P(val));
-                    ZVAL_OBJ(*container, enum_instance);
+                    ZVAL_OBJ_COPY(*container, enum_instance);
 #endif
                     MSGPACK_UNSERIALIZE_FINISH_MAP_ITEM(unpack, key, val);
                     return 0;
